{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"A host firewall is enabled on node1 and persists across restart.","status":"satisfied","summary":"nftables was active and enabled in the default OpenRC runlevel before restart. A restart was acknowledged and observed, the boot ID changed, and nftables returned active with the same configuration checksum and loaded input rules. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-28c089c3972a4651","cmd-209e594b16b84e3c","cmd-bf20990cce9d4b55","cmd-68f0e08bfd084bc9","cmd-29b7e096d2434a20","cmd-5b8dca3a60b945f5","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Inbound SSH on TCP port 22 and application traffic on TCP port 8080 are permitted.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Isolated-ingress tests directly reached active listeners on ports 22 and 8080 before and after restart. The recovered ruleset also explicitly permits new TCP connections to both ports.","evidence_ids":["cmd-37d0ec2ab79d4a16","cmd-5b8dca3a60b945f5","cmd-5e60a0126581401a"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Unrelated inbound connections are rejected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The active ruleset ends with an explicit inbound administrative-prohibited reject after the required allowances. Isolated-ingress testing confirmed that TCP port 9090 was rejected despite an active listener, both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c2dc692b34614cd3","cmd-37d0ec2ab79d4a16","cmd-5b8dca3a60b945f5","cmd-5e60a0126581401a"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"Implementation mutations were causally appropriate: nftables was installed and configured, iproute2 was added as a prerequisite for bounded isolated-ingress verification, and temporary network namespaces/listeners were cleaned up. The failed initial namespace test was a bounded prerequisite-discovery attempt and its transient network/process state was restored. The only identified unnecessary retained mutations are three temporary log artifacts: /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log from the restart command and /tmp/fwtest-8080.log plus /tmp/fwtest-9090.log created or overwritten by the firewall tests; all remained after execution. No test listeners remained, and package-health output was unchanged from the pre-existing baseline.","evidence_ids":["cmd-df79fea9789248c5","cmd-a913a7430499472d","cmd-37d0ec2ab79d4a16","cmd-bf20990cce9d4b55","cmd-5e60a0126581401a","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is strong: it includes a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and disconnection, a different post-restart boot identity, and recovery of sshd, nftables, configuration checksum, rules, and tested traffic behavior. Operational hygiene is good apart from three retained temporary log files.","limitations":["Functional rejection was sampled with TCP port 9090 over the isolated IPv4 ingress path; arbitrary ports, UDP, and IPv6 ingress were not behaviorally tested, although the loaded inet ruleset provides a broad terminal reject.","The lifecycle failed-service probe was unsupported because it checks systemd on an OpenRC host. Direct checks covered the task-relevant nftables and sshd services, but there was no separate general cluster-health probe."]}
